Held-swing speed limit (push method), NOT adopted yet: a patch to pick up later instead of starting over.

What it does: while a block is held, a joint-space swing is slowed so the block's centre never moves faster than
HELD_SWING_MAX_SPEED_MS (m/s; 0 = off, the default it adds).  The path is unchanged, only the duration is
stretched (clearance.held_swing_time; executor.move_arm_to_q gets a `held` argument).  Includes its unit tests.

Why: in push-only games a block swung to the pedestal at 1.67 m/s fell out of the hand; blocks tip more in the
fingers the faster they swing.  At 0.5 m/s it fixed that drop, but overall 29 vs 32 blocks placed in 8 games,
because the pedestal set-down was a coin toss at the time (fixed since: DECISIONS.md D-22).  See O-5.

To try it:   git apply workfiles/held_swing_testing.patch
             then run the push sweep and games with --set HELD_SWING_MAX_SPEED_MS=0.5 (cluster scripts)
Made against the commit that added this file; check with `git apply --check` first.

